# Deterministic line endings on every platform.
#
# tests/audit-article-hash.test.mjs extracts the vendored scorer's
# normalizeMarkdown from its source bytes; a core.autocrlf=true
# checkout (Windows default) must not smudge what tests read. Pin
# every text type we ship to LF so a checkout is byte-identical to
# the repo. (The test also tolerates an already-smudged working
# tree — this file keeps fresh clones clean.)
*.js    text eol=lf
*.mjs   text eol=lf
*.ts    text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf
*.html  text eol=lf
*.css   text eol=lf
*.yml   text eol=lf
*.svg   text eol=lf
*.png   binary

# The JOURNAL is split by month (docs/journal/YYYY-MM.md) and appended
# at the bottom, so two concurrent entries merge cleanly under union.
# Union on the GENERATED index too: a stale PR's prepended entry
# survives the merge instead of conflicting, and `npm run docs:journal`
# moves it into its month — the drift guard (tests/journal-index.test.mjs)
# makes forgetting impossible. What union on the index trades: a
# conflict for a RED DRIFT GUARD, never for silent wrongness — two
# regenerated indexes union in merge order while the generator sorts,
# and main's branch protection (an up-to-date branch before merge) makes
# the second PR's CI run the drift guard on the merged tree — a stale
# index is red there, before it can land; no bot writes to main. Never hand-resolve
# JOURNAL.md: regenerate. A branch from BEFORE the split still gets a
# real conflict when it merges main (git reads this attribute from the
# checked-out side, which lacks it): run `npm run docs:journal` on the
# conflicted file — the markers are boundaries to it — or rebase onto
# main, which unions. Recipes: CONTRIBUTING.md, "Engineering journal".
docs/journal/*.md merge=union
docs/JOURNAL.md   merge=union
